# CustomCard — environment variables (Vite frontend only)
# Copy to .env.local to activate optional features.
# Clerk React auth requires the public Vite publishable key below. Server API
# routes also need Clerk's JWKS public key to verify signed-in session JWTs.
#
# ── Full backend config ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# For Docker / full-stack dev:  infra/env/.env.example  (191 vars, all services)
# For QA / prod:                set vars in Vercel dashboard (environment: Preview / Production)
# Validated at runtime by:      scripts/validate-runtime-env.mjs

# ── Clerk React auth ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
VITE_CLERK_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=pk_test_replace_with_clerk_publishable_key
# Paste Clerk Configure > API keys > JWKS Public Key. This is public
# verification material, but keep real values in .env.local / Vercel env only.
# Encode newlines as \n when storing in a one-line env var.
CLERK_JWT_KEY="-----BEGIN PUBLIC KEY-----\nreplace-with-clerk-jwks-public-key\n-----END PUBLIC KEY-----"
CLERK_AUTHORIZED_PARTIES=http://127.0.0.1:5173,http://localhost:5173,https://your-vercel-domain.example
CLERK_ISSUER=https://your-clerk-issuer.example
CLERK_AUDIENCE=customcard-api

# ── Free legal policy links ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Public URLs generated from free/free-tier policy tools. These are not secrets.
# Leave blank to show the free generator fallback links in the Legal view.
# VITE_LEGAL_TERMS_URL=
# VITE_LEGAL_PRIVACY_URL=
# VITE_LEGAL_COOKIE_URL=
# VITE_LEGAL_REFUND_URL=
# VITE_LEGAL_AI_DISCLOSURE_URL=
# VITE_LEGAL_PRIVACY_CHOICES_URL=

# ── AI card generation sidecar ──────────────────────────────────────────────
# Start the Python sidecar first:
#   cd card_gen && pip install -e . && ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-... uvicorn card_gen.app:app --port 8001
#
# Then set this to show the "Generate with AI" button in Studio:
# VITE_CARD_GEN_URL=http://localhost:8001

# ── Server-only live AI route config ────────────────────────────────────────
# The Node API route can also generate card copy/images directly when these
# values are set in local server env or Vercel env. Do not prefix secrets with
# VITE_.
# CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=replace-me
# CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_TEXT_API_TOKEN=replace-me
# CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_IMAGE_API_TOKEN=replace-me
# CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_TEXT_MODEL=@cf/meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct-fast
# CLOUDFLARE_WORKERS_AI_IMAGE_MODEL=@cf/bytedance/stable-diffusion-xl-lightning
# RUNCOMFY_API_TOKEN=replace-me
# CUSTOMCARD_AI_CARD_IMAGE_ADAPTER_ID=runcomfy-model-api-image
# RunComfy model ids are selected in Admin > Providers. Input schemas vary by model; set
# CUSTOMCARD_RUNCOMFY_IMAGE_INPUT_JSON to override or remove request fields.
# CUSTOMCARD_AI_CARD_COPY_LIVE_ENABLED=true
# CUSTOMCARD_AI_CARD_IMAGE_LIVE_ENABLED=true

# ── Server-only Google Calendar OAuth start ─────────────────────────────────
# Enables the Google Calendar button to return a live Google consent URL from
# /api/calendar/connections/start. Keep the secret server-side only.
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_ID=replace-with-google-web-client-id.apps.googleusercontent.com
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_CLIENT_SECRET=replace-with-google-client-secret
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=replace-with-32-plus-character-state-secret
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-32-plus-character-token-encryption-key
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:5173/oauth/callback
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=replace-with-random-32-byte-secret
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_STATE_SECRET=replace-with-random-state-signing-secret
# GOOGLE_CALENDAR_IMPORT_MAX_RESULTS=10
# Production redirect URI:
# GOOGLE_OAUTH_REDIRECT_URI=https://customcard-three.vercel.app/oauth/callback

# ── Server-only Walgreens hosted checkout production ────────────────────────
# Enables /api/walgreens/checkout/* to call the Walgreens hosted-checkout
# production API. Do not prefix these with VITE_; never commit real values.
# The API key and AffiliateID are both required by Walgreens.
# WALGREENS_VENDOR_MODE=production
# WALGREENS_API_KEY=replace-with-walgreens-api-key
# WALGREENS_AFF_ID=replace-with-walgreens-affiliate-id
# WALGREENS_PUBLISHER_ID=
# PUBLIC_APP_ORIGIN=http://127.0.0.1:5173

# ── Server-only object store ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# R2/S3 render-packet persistence is server-side only. Do not expose the S3
# access keys through Vite variables. Configure OBJECT_STORE_* in
# infra/env/.env for Docker/local API work and in Vercel Project Settings for
# hosted API routes.

# ── Server-only provider worker HTTP bridge ────────────────────────────────
# Hosted API: set the SHA-256 hash of the raw local worker token. The local
# worker gets only the raw token plus local Comfy/LLM env, not DATABASE_URL or
# R2 writer credentials.
# CUSTOMCARD_PROVIDER_WORKER_TOKEN_SHA256=replace-with-sha256-of-local-token
# CUSTOMCARD_PROVIDER_WORKER_ROUTE_IDS=ai-card-generate
# CUSTOMCARD_PROVIDER_WORKER_LEASE_SECONDS=300
#
# Local provider machine:
# CUSTOMCARD_PROVIDER_API_BASE_URL=https://your-vercel-domain.example
# CUSTOMCARD_PROVIDER_WORKER_TOKEN=replace-with-32-plus-character-token
# CUSTOMCARD_WORKER_ID=manny-comfy-01
